      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patients with chronic calculous cholecystitis presenting with atherosclerotic affliction of the heart reveal impairement of the mechanism of adaptation. A trigger mechanism in the activation of the hypophysial-adrenal system is, on the hand, a stressful impact on the frontal lobe of hypophysis and as a consequence of this a pain pang on the adrenal cortex accompanied by tissue hypoxia; on the other hand, disorders in the intrahepatic circulation of bile, enzymic disfunction of hepatocytes result, in their turn, in hypercholesterinemia which promotes augmentation of hydrocortisone levels. A quercetin-pectin complex has been proposed combined with SKN-type enterosorbent to correct the above disorders."},
